      { s: "", jp: "{本当|ほんとう}の{自由|じゆう}とは、{自|みずか}ら{定|さだ}めた{規範|きはん}に{従|したが}って{行動|こうどう}できることだという{考|かんが}え{方|かた}である。", ro: "Hontō no jiyū to wa, mizukara sadameta kihan ni shitagatte kōdō dekiru koto da toiu kangae kata dearu.", en: "The view is that true freedom is being able to act according to norms one has set oneself." },
      { s: "", jp: "たとえば、{好|す}きなだけ{食|た}べ{続|つづ}けて{体|からだ}を{壊|こわ}す{人|ひと}は、{自分|じぶん}の{意志|いし}で{動|うご}いているとは{言|い}いにくい。", ro: "Tatoeba, sukina dake tabetsuzukete karada o kowasu hito wa, jibun no ishi de ugoite iru to wa iinikui.", en: "For example, a person who keeps eating as much as he likes and ruins his health can hardly be said to be moving by his own will." },
      { s: "", jp: "この{見方|みかた}に{立|た}てば、{他人|たにん}の{自由|じゆう}を{尊重|そんちょう}することも、{自分|じぶん}の{自由|じゆう}の{条件|じょうけん}の{一部|いちぶ}となる。", ro: "Kono mikata ni tateba, tanin no jiyū o sonchō suru koto mo, jibun no jiyū no jōken no ichibu to naru.", en: "From this standpoint, respecting others' freedom also becomes part of the conditions of one's own freedom." },
      { s: "", jp: "{自由|じゆう}と{責任|せきにん}は{対立|たいりつ}するのではなく、{表裏一体|ひょうりいったい}の{関係|かんけい}にあるのだ。", ro: "Jiyū to sekinin wa tairitsu suru node wa naku, hyōriittai no kankei ni aru no da.", en: "Freedom and responsibility do not conflict; they stand in a relationship of two sides of one coin." },
      { s: "", jp: "{制約|せいやく}を{受|う}け{入|い}れることは、{自由|じゆう}の{喪失|そうしつ}ではなく、むしろその{成熟|せいじゅく}の{証|あかし}でもある。", ro: "Seiyaku o ukeireru koto wa, jiyū no sōshitsu de wa naku, mushiro sono seijuku no akashi de mo aru.", en: "Accepting restraint is not a loss of freedom but rather also a sign of its maturity." }
